cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HyperMix: open detection of engineered biosignatures in remote hyperspectral imagery"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "João Victor"
    family-names: Dias
repository-code: "https://github.com/JVLegend/HyperMix"
url: "https://github.com/JVLegend/HyperMix"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-07-18
keywords:
  - hyperspectral
  - remote sensing
  - biosensing
  - target detection
  - spectral unmixing
  - synthetic biology
abstract: >-
  An open benchmark toolkit for detecting engineered biosignatures in remote
  hyperspectral imagery, with calibrated uncertainty. It includes a
  physics-based simulator, implanted-target benchmarks on real airborne
  backgrounds, classical baselines and learned models. In the completed
  detection experiments, no learned method robustly outperforms a
  well-calibrated spatial matched filter. Evaluation on physically measured
  bioHSI targets is paused pending recovery of the manual Figure 4g
  coordinates. Developed under the Experiment Foundation Hyperspectral Biology
  grant.
